<title>FRANCE: TENNIS-LATEST FRENCH OPEN WOMEN'S RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-LATEST FRENCH OPEN WOMEN'S RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Women's singles results in the</p>
<p>French Open tennis tournament on Monday.</p>
<p>Prefix number denotes seeding</p>
<p>* Denotes new result</p>
<p>First round:</p>
<p>*Patty Schnyder (Switzerland) beat Marion Maruska (Austria) 6-3</p>
<p>6-3</p>
<p>*Helena Sukova (Czech Republic) beat Sandra Dopfer (Austria) 6-3</p>
<p>6-4</p>
<p>*5-Lindsay Davenport (U.S.) beat Joannette Kruger (South Africa)</p>
<p>6-2 6-3</p>
<p>Magui Serna (Spain) beat Linda Wild (U.S.) 7-6 (7-4) 6-0</p>
<p>9-Iva Majoli (Croatia) beat Sandra Kleinova (Czech Republic) 7-5</p>
<p>6-4</p>
<p>Caroline Dhenin (France) beat Sabine Appelmans (Belgium) 6-7</p>
<p>(7-9) 6-2 6-1</p>
<p>Yayuk Basuki (Indonesia) beat Asa Carlsson (Sweden) 6-4 4-6 6-1</p>
<p>Venus Williams (U.S.) beat Naoko Sawamatsu (Japan) 6-2  6-7</p>
<p>(2-7) 7-5</p>
<p>Chanda Rubin (U.S.) beat Mariana Diaz-oliva (Argentina) 7-6</p>
<p>(7-5) 7-5</p>
<p>Silvija Talaja (Croatia) beat Marketa Kochta (Germany)  7-5 6-3</p>
<p>Ines Gorrochategui (Argentina) beat Aleksandra Olsza (Poland)</p>
<p>6-3 6-3</p>
<p>Amy Frazier (U.S.) beat Denisa Chladkova (Czech Republic) 6-4</p>
<p>6-0</p>
<p>Nicole Arendt (U.S.) beat Rika Hiraki (Japan) 6-2 6-1</p>
<p>Alexandra Fusai (France) beat Ludmila Richterova (Czech</p>
<p>Republic)  7-5 3-0 retired injured</p>
<p>11-Amanda Coetzer (South Africa) beat Rita Grande (Italy) 6-4</p>
<p>6-0</p>
</text>
